{"success":true,"data":{"origin":"http://127.0.0.1:8000/","result":{"brief":[{"hidden":false,"id":"scenario","text":"Happy pathLose acknowledgement after effectLose acknowledgement before effectContradictory observationLow-confidence observationStale observationLogical E-stopCell faultInvalid Brain outputBrain timeoutDuplicate command deliveryBroker temporarily unavailableEdge temporarily unavailableOPC UA connection interruptionController restart after executionWMS unavailable after verified pick"},{"hidden":false,"id":"scenario-brief","text":"Normal pick: move the product, receive the reply and check its new position."},{"hidden":false,"id":"scenario-watch","text":"The product reaches the output tote and the job becomes COMPLETED."},{"hidden":false,"id":"scenario-scope","text":"Applied when you create and run a new order. Observation faults here affect that order's first check after the pick."},{"hidden":false,"id":"scenario-phase","text":"Whole pick · no injected fault"},{"hidden":false,"id":"scenario-meaning","text":"The baseline test: the planner supplies a valid plan, the controller moves the product and replies, and a fresh observation checks the result."},{"hidden":false,"id":"scenario-difference","text":"Use this to compare normal operation with a test that deliberately breaks one part of the workflow."},{"hidden":false,"id":"scenario-help","text":"Expected: the machine moves the product to the destination and fresh evidence confirms completion."},{"hidden":false,"id":"scenario-compare","text":"Compare all execution scenarios\n    ScenarioWhat changesHappy pathWhole pick · no injected faultThe baseline test: the planner supplies a valid plan, the controller moves the product and replies, and a fresh observation checks the result.Lose acknowledgement after effectCommunication · after movementAn acknowledgement is the controller's reply about a command. Here the pick happens and is recorded, but that reply is deliberately lost on its way back.Lose acknowledgement before effectCommunication · no movement startedThe controller records that the pick never started, and its reply is deliberately lost. The orchestrator receives no confirmation of that no-effect outcome.Contradictory observationVerification · first check after movementAfter the pick, the simulated observation reports the same product in two different locations, such as source and destination. This tests handling of mutually conflicting detections.Low-confidence observationVerification · first check after movementAfter the pick, the observation includes the product and a location, but its confidence score is deliberately reduced. This tests whether weak evidence is refused.Stale observationVerification · first check after movementSimulates delayed sensing by giving the post-pick observation an old capture time. Its location report may look plausible, but it is too old to establish the current outcome.Logical E-stopCell control · before movementSimulates a deliberate stop request, like an operator pressing the simulator's stop control. The cell enters a stopped state and refuses the pick until reset. This is not safety-rated.Cell faultCell control · before movementSimulates the controller detecting a cell error before movement. It marks the cell faulted and refuses the pick until the logical state is reset.Invalid Brain outputPlanning · before command creationThe Brain is the pick planner. This test supplies a reply that does not match the required action-plan format, so validation rejects it before a robot command can be created.Duplicate command deliveryTransport · repeated original identityDelivers the same immutable command identity again to the edge inbox. The inbox and PLC must recognize its payload hash and retain the original result.Broker temporarily unavailableOutbox · before distributed deliveryMakes the first bounded publication attempt unavailable. The committed command and outbox remain available for an explicit retry.Edge temporarily unavailableDelivery · durable inbox boundaryMakes the first edge-delivery stage unavailable. Publisher confirmation alone does not establish that the edge stored the command.OPC UA connection interruptionController session · before acceptanceInjects an unavailable controller connection on the first session-stage attempt. Local mode models this boundary; lab mode uses an actual OPC UA client/server for the successful retry.Controller restart after executionController result · original durable journalRestarts the virtual controller state after motion, then queries the original command. Lab mode changes the PLC boot identity through its restart method; local mode reloads the simulated runtime from durable storage.WMS unavailable after verified pickBusiness reconciliation · after verificationThe robot completes and fresh evidence verifies the pick, but the first WMS acknowledgement attempt is unavailable.Brain timeoutPlanning · before command creationSimulates the pick planner missing its response deadline. The workflow handles the timeout before creating a robot command.\n    Descriptions assume the standard test settings. The recorded evidence determines the actual outcome.\n  "},{"hidden":false,"id":"scenario-comparisons","text":"Happy pathWhole pick · no injected faultThe baseline test: the planner supplies a valid plan, the controller moves the product and replies, and a fresh observation checks the result.Lose acknowledgement after effectCommunication · after movementAn acknowledgement is the controller's reply about a command. Here the pick happens and is recorded, but that reply is deliberately lost on its way back.Lose acknowledgement before effectCommunication · no movement startedThe controller records that the pick never started, and its reply is deliberately lost. The orchestrator receives no confirmation of that no-effect outcome.Contradictory observationVerification · first check after movementAfter the pick, the simulated observation reports the same product in two different locations, such as source and destination. This tests handling of mutually conflicting detections.Low-confidence observationVerification · first check after movementAfter the pick, the observation includes the product and a location, but its confidence score is deliberately reduced. This tests whether weak evidence is refused.Stale observationVerification · first check after movementSimulates delayed sensing by giving the post-pick observation an old capture time. Its location report may look plausible, but it is too old to establish the current outcome.Logical E-stopCell control · before movementSimulates a deliberate stop request, like an operator pressing the simulator's stop control. The cell enters a stopped state and refuses the pick until reset. This is not safety-rated.Cell faultCell control · before movementSimulates the controller detecting a cell error before movement. It marks the cell faulted and refuses the pick until the logical state is reset.Invalid Brain outputPlanning · before command creationThe Brain is the pick planner. This test supplies a reply that does not match the required action-plan format, so validation rejects it before a robot command can be created.Duplicate command deliveryTransport · repeated original identityDelivers the same immutable command identity again to the edge inbox. The inbox and PLC must recognize its payload hash and retain the original result.Broker temporarily unavailableOutbox · before distributed deliveryMakes the first bounded publication attempt unavailable. The committed command and outbox remain available for an explicit retry.Edge temporarily unavailableDelivery · durable inbox boundaryMakes the first edge-delivery stage unavailable. Publisher confirmation alone does not establish that the edge stored the command.OPC UA connection interruptionController session · before acceptanceInjects an unavailable controller connection on the first session-stage attempt. Local mode models this boundary; lab mode uses an actual OPC UA client/server for the successful retry.Controller restart after executionController result · original durable journalRestarts the virtual controller state after motion, then queries the original command. Lab mode changes the PLC boot identity through its restart method; local mode reloads the simulated runtime from durable storage.WMS unavailable after verified pickBusiness reconciliation · after verificationThe robot completes and fresh evidence verifies the pick, but the first WMS acknowledgement attempt is unavailable.Brain timeoutPlanning · before command creationSimulates the pick planner missing its response deadline. The workflow handles the timeout before creating a robot command."},{"hidden":false,"id":"motion-scenario","text":"New delivery · ready for the selected scenario."}],"create":{"disabled":false,"id":"create"},"live":{"live":{"at":"2026-10-06T03:57:46.027Z","buttons":{"advance":{"disabled":true,"hidden":false,"text":"Continue"},"reconcile":{"disabled":false,"hidden":true,"text":"Reconcile original command"}},"commandId":null,"correlationId":null,"jobId":null,"lastStep":null,"miniMapCurrent":[],"orderId":null,"pendingStage":null,"physicalAuthorized":false,"playback":{"cursor":0,"disabled":{"motion-play":true,"motion-replay":true,"motion-scrub":true,"motion-speed":true,"motion-step-back":true,"motion-step-forward":true},"executionGated":false,"playing":false},"readOnly":false,"revision":null,"selectedInspectorStage":null,"selectedSession":"","sessionId":null,"stage":null,"status":null,"stepCount":0,"uiBusy":false,"uiError":null},"phase":null,"postCount":0,"storageWarning":null,"version":"manual-proof-v1"},"scenario":""}},"error":null}
